cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "tptp"
abstract: >-
  tptp is a span-preserving parser, linter and printer for the TPTP language in
  Elixir, generated from the published TPTP syntax BNF (v9.3.1.3). It also
  carries the SZS ontologies, generated from the TPTP World's SZSOntology.bnf,
  with their isa hierarchy. It has no runtime dependencies and performs no
  elaboration or type checking.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Schuster
    given-names: Johannes
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-5339-7216"
    affiliation: "Otto-Friedrich-Universität Bamberg, Germany"
version: "0.1.2"
date-released: "2026-09-30"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jcschuster/tptp"
url: "https://hexdocs.pm/tptp"
keywords:
  - TPTP
  - parser
  - linter
  - pretty-printer
  - BNF
  - SZS
  - automated reasoning
  - Elixir
  - BEAM
